                <head>224. Telegram From the Presidentʼs Special Assistant (Rostow) to President
                    Johnson in Texas<anchor n="1" xml:id="d224-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1967-12-29">December 29, 1967</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>CAP 671233. Herewith the message I have just dispatched via back channel, in your
                    name, to Ambassador Bowles, as instructed by Jim Jones.</p>
                <p>In my four years of the Presidency, I have asked very little, if anything, of the
                    Indian Governments. I am asking something now; namely, that at the highest level
                    they make a maximum effort, through the ICC, to end Communist use of Cambodian
                    territory.</p>
                <p>I believe the Indians sincerely want peace in Southeast Asia and desire authentic
                    neutral status. This is the time for them to act in terms of both
                    objectives.</p>
                <p>Unless the ICC can, at last, perform effectively in the case of Cambodia, the war
                    may well spread.</p>
                <p>India should now move promptly and effectively to prevent this.</p>
                <p>I count on you to devote full time, if necessary, to this task.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
